The Sentinel is the good elite of the Warden (ranger route, alignment +30 at
promotion). It watches the line: when a foe can reach an ally in the middle or
back row, the Sentinel holds its turn and shoots the first foe that strikes
one of them. It needs a shooting weapon.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Overwatch         holds its turn when a foe can reach its middle
                       or back row; the first foe that strikes one of
                       those allies is shot before the blow resolves,
                       and on a hit the blow lands at half damage
  35 Steady overwatch  the Overwatch shot has +5 Attack
  40 Pull down         an Overwatch hit knocks down a leaping foe
  45 Watchful          back-row allies have +5 Evasion while the
                       Sentinel stands
  50 Spoil the chant   Overwatch also answers a foe beginning a chant;
                       a hit breaks the chant
  55 Twin watch        Overwatch can fire twice a round; the second
                       shot spends the Sentinel's next turn too
  60 Guardian Arrow    an Overwatch hit stops the blow entirely

Overwatch is a class ability, listed first in <ansi
fg="command">strategy</ansi> and held back by <ansi fg="command">strategy
[member] abilities off</ansi>. A held turn that sees no strike is simply
spent. It never advances the shared clock.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Ranger elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Long Draw (+10% damage with a
shooting weapon), Eagle Eye (+5 Attack with a shooting weapon), Quick Nock
(+15 opening action meter). Every elite ranger may take them. See <ansi
fg="command">help talents</ansi>.


See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help ranger-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
